<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_ExtremeDesert                              UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. R22 stands (`_freeze_rulings_2026-09-07.md`): the dune sea
    and the deep desert stay ONE owned def, merging design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
    dune_sea.md and deep_desert.md (both FROZEN). Splitting them is cheap once owned
    but is the OWNER's call to reopen, not authored here.

    MEASURED: dune_sea.md's SS2 puts the merged def's arc band at roughly theta 0-45
    deg (deep dayside, +70 C at the substellar point falling toward +52 C at theta 40);
    deep_desert.md's SS0 table (region-level, partly superseded by repaint per its own
    Owed note) names the far ring past the Pyrelands. Tile count is not restated
    here — it is repainted by world edits and drifts; read it live from
    `world/ASHKARR_WORLDMAP_tiles.csv`.

    allowRoads FALSE, overriding the general "all our biomes allow roads" ruling
    (RUT_NightsideIce/RUT_TheScald's own comment): dune_sea.md SS6 carries an explicit
    named ban — "No roads through the deep dune (owner's ruling on the Deep Desert
    Tribes)." A sheet-specific hard ban outranks the general default.

    Weather: dune_sea.md SS6 bans standing water/ice/fog/rain "of any kind" and bans
    fire outright (no fuel) — Fog/Rain/RainyThunderstorm/FoggyRain/Snow all zeroed.
    Clear dominant ("the light is a fixed condition... one source, hard, high,
    unmoving" SS9). DryThunderstorm kept minimal (dry only, no fuel to ignite — SS6
    "No fire. There is no fuel"). Sandstorm (Odyssey) kept: the one unidirectional
    wind that never reverses (SS2) is the biome's whole engine.

    plantDensity/animalDensity kept at the donor's own near-zero values
    (0.008/0.1): dune_sea.md's own "Roster consequences" section rules it explicitly —
    "Population target: sparse to the point of discomfort... If the dune sea's roster
    looks healthy, it is wrong."

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml (generated against rosters/dune_sea_deep_desert.json, the
    ONE merged roster file R22 already ruled).

    NOT this pass's scope: the Silverbole tree def (deep_desert.md SS4b, name still
    owner's pick); the sarlacc (deep_desert.md Owed, its own item); the megafauna
    filter-feeders and glass-nub light-pipe flora (both sheets' SS4/SS10, new-art
    owed); the wind-grain/yardang map-gen routine; any world repaint.

    WYYYSCHOKK_FERALISK_MERGE_1 (2026-09-10): AA_Dunealisk removed from
    wildAnimals: owner sitting ruling retired Alpha Animals' whole '-lisk'
    clade (Cherry Picker cut); the defName stops resolving once that cut
    takes effect, and an unresolved cross-ref in wildAnimals is a known
    crash (BIOME_CAST_REFS_BREAK_MAPGEN_1).

  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_ExtremeDesert</defName>
    <label>the Extreme Desert</label>
    <description>A corrugated ochre plain under a star that has not moved since the world began, running unbroken to every horizon. Nothing here tracks the sun because the sun does not go anywhere; everything owns a shadow instead, or is buried, or is a giant carrying its own moving shade across a thousand kilometres of nothing. It ends, without a gradient, at a hard green line of river or sea -- and until then, this is the ocean of nothing that line is drawn against.</description>
    <workerClass>RimWorld.BiomeWorker_ExtremeDesert</workerClass>
    <settleWarning>Searing heat and a near total lack of arable land make survival here a challenge. Nothing here pursues, but nothing here forgives a mistake either.</settleWarning>
    <isExtremeBiome>true</isExtremeBiome>
    <hasVirtualPlants>false</hasVirtualPlants>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>Sand</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <mudTerrain>Sand</mudTerrain>
    <riverbankTerrain>Sand</riverbankTerrain>
    <allowRoads>false</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>0.1</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.008</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>World/Biomes/ExtremeDesert</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>90</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>40</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>40</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_OrganDecay</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>10</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Sand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>95</Clear>
      <DryThunderstorm>1</DryThunderstorm>
      <Fog>0</Fog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <Sandstorm MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">4</Sandstorm>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <RSW_Scavrat MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.6</RSW_Scavrat>  <!-- Scavrats - ship-vermin, import -->
      <RSW_WompRat MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.4</RSW_WompRat>  <!-- womp rat - ship-vermin, import -->
      <RSW_Mynock MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Mynock>  <!-- mynock - ship-vermin, import -->
      <RSW_Cindermite MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Cindermite>  <!-- fuelmite - ship-vermin, import -->
      <RSW_Spineroller MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_Spineroller>  <!-- needleroll - grain-scale, adjust-keep -->
      <RSW_Kreetle MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_Kreetle>  <!-- kreetle - grain-scale, keep -->
      <RSW_WarWyrm MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_WarWyrm>  <!-- war wyrm - giant, keep -->
      <RSW_KraytDragon MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.15</RSW_KraytDragon>  <!-- krayt dragon - giant, keep -->
      <RSW_Stareling MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.15</RSW_Stareling>  <!-- ikee - grain-scale, adjust-keep -->
      <Rat>0.1</Rat>  <!-- brown rat - ship-vermin, import -->
      <RSW_GraniteSlug MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_GraniteSlug>  <!-- granite slug - grain-scale, keep -->
      <RSW_Scurrier MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RSW_Scurrier>  <!-- scurrier - grain-scale, adjust-keep -->
      <!-- DROID_DEPOT_REPOINT 2026-09-20 (owner: "Droid depot is our custom mod we are
           building"). These 7 were pointing at neronix17.outerrim.droiddepot, which is NOT
           in the active mod list - MayRequire-guarded, so they silently never spawned.
           Our own Droidworks already absorbed them as RSW_DW_OuterRim_*Droid PawnKindDefs
           (src/RimStarWars/Droidworks/Defs/PawnKinds_OuterRim.xml, generated by
           gen_droidworks_defs.py). Repointed; commonalities unchanged. -->
      <RSW_DW_OuterRim_MSEDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.1</RSW_DW_OuterRim_MSEDroid>  <!-- MSE Repair Droid - feral-droid, import -->
      <RSW_DW_OuterRim_SalvageAssistDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.1</RSW_DW_OuterRim_SalvageAssistDroid>  <!-- salvage assist droid - feral-droid, import -->
      <RSW_DW_OuterRim_DUMDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.08</RSW_DW_OuterRim_DUMDroid>  <!-- DUM Repair Droid - feral-droid, import -->
      <RSW_DW_OuterRim_GNKDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.08</RSW_DW_OuterRim_GNKDroid>  <!-- GNK Power Droid - feral-droid, import -->
      <RSW_DW_OuterRim_FX7Droid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.05</RSW_DW_OuterRim_FX7Droid>  <!-- fx-7 medical droid - feral-droid, import -->
      <RSW_DW_OuterRim_MuckrakerDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.05</RSW_DW_OuterRim_MuckrakerDroid>  <!-- Muckraker Crab Droid - feral-droid, import -->
      <RSW_Stoneback MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.025</RSW_Stoneback>  <!-- bouldermit - giant, keep -->
      <RSW_DW_OuterRim_DestroyerDroid MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.droidworks">0.02</RSW_DW_OuterRim_DestroyerDroid>  <!-- Destroyer Droid - feral-droid, import -->
      <RSW_Gizka MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.01</RSW_Gizka>  <!-- gizka - grain-scale, keep -->
      <RSW_GreaterKraytDragon MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.001</RSW_GreaterKraytDragon>  <!-- greater krayt dragon - giant, keep -->
      <RSW_Voltmaw MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.0005</RSW_Voltmaw>  <!-- tetra slug - giant, keep -->
      <!-- DESERT_ROUND2_IMPORTS_UNLANDED_1 2026-09-20: round-2 import row
           (rosters/dune_sea_deep_desert.json "fauna", owner review 2026-09, commonality
           0.5), wired for the first time. -->
      <RSW_TruffleMole MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_TruffleMole>  <!-- truffle mole - sand burrower, desert & extreme desert, import -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <RSW_Plant_Bloddle MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.05</RSW_Plant_Bloddle>  <!-- bloddle plant -->
      <!-- AB_GiantStikehr REMOVED 2026-09-20 on the owner's eye ("The giant mushroom seems
           misplaced"). Alpha Biomes' own description makes it a Forsaken Crags organism: "A
           giant alien mushroom that glows in the strange darkening mist... as long as it is
           protected by the Forsaken [Crags]". It is correctly carried there at 0.3
           (RUT_ForsakenCrags.xml). A glowing mist-mushroom on the hottest, driest, sunniest
           biome on the planet was a stray copy - the entry carried no rationale comment,
           unlike every other row here. ⚠️ This leaves Plant_Bloddle as the ONLY wildPlant on
           3,969 tiles; sparse is this sheet's intent ("if the roster looks healthy, it is
           wrong") but one species is thin even for that - tracked on DESERT_FAMILY_VERDICT_PASS_1. -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>35</wildPlantRegrowDays>

    <!-- DESERT_PACK_ANIMALS_FOR_TRADERS_1 (owner, 2026-09-20: both deserts get traders).
         allowedPackAnimals was absent (= empty list), so PawnGroupKindWorker_Trader.
         CanGenerateFrom returned false and no trader caravan ever generated here.
         MEASURED: all five ported herd beasts carry <packAnimal>true</packAnimal> in
         their ThingDef (src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RSW_{Bantha,
         Ronto,Eopie,Jamel,Falumpaset}.xml), so all five are listed — same set as
         RUT_Desert, per the owner's ruling. -->
    <allowedPackAnimals>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Bantha</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Ronto</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Eopie</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Jamel</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Falumpaset</li>
    </allowedPackAnimals>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
